; File/layer: tests/fake_j2534.def | export-name control for the fake vendor DLL
; Testing: N/A (linker input)
;
; WHY THIS EXISTS: on x86, MSVC decorates __stdcall exports as
; _PassThruOpen@8 etc., so GetProcAddress("PassThruOpen") fails — the
; cross-arch surrogate surfaced this (exit code 5, 2026-10-14). The
; real J2534-1 spec likewise requires undecorated export names; vendor
; DLLs use def files for the same reason. Bare names in EXPORTS force
; undecorated exports on BOTH x86 and x64.
;
; Part 4 additions: PassThruStartMsgFilter / PassThruStopMsgFilter
; (now spec-mandatory members of the nine-export table BOTH backends
; resolve) and the three new observation hooks. Without the filter
; entries here, an x86 surrogate hosting this fake dies at exit 5 on
; export resolution — the exact Part 2 trap pointed at the new set.

LIBRARY fake_j2534
EXPORTS
    PassThruOpen
    PassThruClose
    PassThruConnect
    PassThruDisconnect
    PassThruReadMsgs
    PassThruWriteMsgs
    PassThruIoCtl
    PassThruStartMsgFilter
    PassThruStopMsgFilter
    InjectFrame
    GetBufferState
    GetCurrentHandle
    GetLastConnectParams
    GetWriteCount
    GetRecordedWrite
    GetLastFilterStart
    